  "privacyNoticeTitle": "Camera privacy",
  "privacyNoticeBody": "Posture Guard can use your front camera to help check your posture while you use your phone.",
  "privacyNoticeDetail": "Camera images are processed on your device only. They are not saved or uploaded. You can turn camera assistance off at any time and continue monitoring with your phone's angle sensors.",
  "useSensorsOnly": "Use sensors only",
  "cameraAssistTitle": "Use camera to help detect posture",
  "cameraAssistSettingDescription": "Optional front-camera assistance while this app is visible. Sensor monitoring works without it.",
  "cameraExplanationTitle": "Camera assistance",
  "cameraExplanationBody": "Posture Guard can use your front camera to help improve posture detection while the app is open.\n\nCamera images are processed on your device, are not saved, and are not uploaded.\n\nCamera access is optional. If you choose not to allow it, posture monitoring will continue using your phone's motion sensors.",
  "notNow": "Not now",
  "cameraActiveIndicator": "Front camera active",
  "cameraAndPrivacy": "Privacy & PDPA",
  "privacyInformationBody": "The front camera may be used only as an optional posture signal while this app is visible and posture monitoring needs extra help. Images are processed on this device, discarded after analysis, and are never saved or uploaded. You can always use sensor-only monitoring.",
  "privacyPageIntroduction": "How Posture Guard handles your data and the privacy choices available to you.",
  "privacyPagePostureTitle": "Posture and motion data",
  "privacyPagePostureBody": "Posture Guard reads motion and orientation sensor values to estimate your phone angle and posture. Current sensor samples are processed while monitoring; raw sensor streams are not saved and do not provide your location. The app stores only your calibration and the daily aggregate posture statistics described below.",
  "privacyPageCameraUseTitle": "Camera use",
  "privacyPageCameraUseIntroduction": "Camera assistance is optional. When it is enabled:",
  "privacyPageCameraUseItems": "Posture Guard selects the front-facing camera to assist posture detection.\nFace position is used for posture assistance, not to recognize or identify you.\nFrames are processed on this device and discarded after analysis.\nFrames are never saved or uploaded to Firebase or another server.\nAn in-app indicator appears whenever camera assistance is active.",
  "privacyPageCameraUseClosing": "You can turn camera assistance off at any time and continue in sensor-only mode.",
  "privacyPageCameraPermissionTitle": "Camera permission",
  "privacyPageCameraPermissionBody": "The first-run disclosure does not request camera permission. Your device's permission prompt appears only after you choose to enable camera assistance. You can deny or later revoke access in device settings; sensor-only monitoring will continue.",
  "privacyPageDataStoredTitle": "Data kept on this device",
  "privacyPageDataStoredIntroduction": "To work offline and restore your choices, Posture Guard keeps:",
  "privacyPageDataStoredItems": "Monitoring and reminder settings, including temporary alert mute\nPosture calibration and daily aggregate posture history\nAndroid aggregate screen time, only if you enable Usage Access\nCoin balance and award dates\nOwned and equipped cosmetics\nSelected language, tutorial status, privacy choice, and camera-assistance preference",
  "privacyPageDataStoredClosing": "Raw motion samples and camera frames are not stored.",
  "privacyPageFirebaseTitle": "Firebase and cloud data",
  "privacyPageFirebaseBody": "Posture Guard uses Firebase Anonymous Authentication. It does not ask for a name, email address, or password, and the anonymous UID is used only to separate each user's cloud data.\n\nUnder users/{uid}, Firebase Realtime Database synchronizes monitoring and reminder settings, calibration, daily aggregate monitoring and posture statistics, alert and availability counts, Android aggregate screen time when enabled, coin balance and award dates, and owned cosmetic IDs. Equipped cosmetics, language, tutorial status, and camera choices stay local. Camera frames and raw motion samples are never uploaded.",
  "privacyPageScreenTimeTitle": "Device screen time",
  "privacyPageScreenTimeAndroidBody": "On Android, Usage Access is optional. Posture Guard filters Android usage events to screen-interactive and screen-non-interactive events to calculate today's total interactive screen time. Package names and per-app activity are not used by the app and do not cross into Flutter. Only the resulting aggregate duration is stored locally and synchronized with daily statistics. If you deny access, Posture Guard shows its own monitored time instead.",
  "privacyPageScreenTimeIosBody": "Whole-device screen time is not available in the current iOS app. Posture Guard shows only the time it monitored while active and does not request Android Usage Access on iOS.",
  "privacyPageChoicesTitle": "Alerts, permissions, and your choices",
  "privacyPageChoicesItems": "Turn Posture Guard monitoring off in Settings.\nUse sensor-only mode, disable camera assistance, or deny or revoke camera access.\nTurn posture reminders off in the app or disable notifications in device settings. Notifications contain a short posture reminder, not camera frames or sensor samples.\nOn Android, deny or remove optional Usage Access.\nReview Privacy & PDPA or choose Delete my data from Settings at any time.",
  "privacyPageDeleteTitle": "Delete your data",
  "privacyPageDeleteBody": "Delete my data removes the users/{uid} cloud node and anonymous Firebase account, then clears user-scoped local settings, calibration, statistics and screen-time cache, coins, cosmetics, tutorial state, privacy choice, and camera preference. Your selected language and OS permission-prompt history remain so the app does not unexpectedly ask again. If a stage fails, the app reports it and keeps the pending cleanup safe to retry.",
  "privacyPageCameraIndicatorTitle": "Camera indicator",
  "privacyPageCameraIndicatorBody": "Whenever the front camera is actually active for posture assistance, Posture Guard displays an in-app camera activity indicator.\n\nThis lets you know when the camera is being used.",
  "privacyPageConsentTitle": "Consent and control",
  "privacyPageConsentBody": "Camera assistance is optional and requires your permission.\n\nChoosing not to use the camera does not prevent you from using Posture Guard's main sensor-based posture monitoring.\n\nYou can change your choice at any time in Settings.",
  "privacyPagePolicyTitle": "About PDPA",
  "privacyPagePolicyBody": "This Privacy & PDPA page is a plain-language summary of how the current app handles data and the controls available to you. It is informational and is not a certification or guarantee of legal compliance.",
